#: ../../../../README.md:2478
msgid "About"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../README.md:2480
msgid ""
"PyGMT is a library for processing geospatial and geophysical data and making "
"publication-quality maps and figures. It provides a Pythonic interface for "
"the [Generic Mapping Tools (GMT)](https://github.com/GenericMappingTools/"
"gmt), a command-line program widely used across the Earth, Ocean, and "
"Planetary sciences and beyond."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../README.md:2485
msgid "Project goals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../README.md:2487
msgid "Make GMT more accessible to new users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../README.md:2488
msgid "Build a Pythonic API for GMT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../README.md:2489
msgid "Interface with the GMT C API directly using ctypes (no system calls)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../README.md:2490
msgid "Support for rich display in the Jupyter notebook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../README.md:2491
msgid ""
"Integration with the [scientific Python ecosystem](https://scientific-python."
"org/): `numpy.ndarray` or `pandas.DataFrame` for data tables, `xarray."
"DataArray` for grids, and `geopandas.GeoDataFrame` for geographical data."
msgstr ""

